    {
      "id": "msg_069fff3193f3fb85016af7d7c762c087d1911028ffda09c191",
      "content": [
        {
          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"ddd2f5a8191c1ae70b57ec33\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"task_requirements\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Required: the no-service request must be investigated sufficiently to establish whether the agent can resolve it before transfer.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0004\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"}],\"rationale\":\"Identify the customer, use device-grounded diagnostics, and follow the SIM troubleshooting rule. On the chosen path, a missing SIM is reseated before its locked state becomes the decisive escalation condition.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":2,\"information\":2}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_001\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Selected conditional endpoint: transfer is appropriate once the locked SIM is established, rather than treating the reference call as proof that transfer is immediately permitted.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0314\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}],\"rationale\":\"The locked-SIM rule calls for escalation. The agent must make the transfer call with a summary and then give the prescribed transfer message.\",\"applicability\":\"selected_conditional\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":1,\"tool_use\":1,\"information\":1}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"This is one support objective with several stages: customer lookup, device diagnosis, a plausible initial airplane-mode correction, SIM reseating when missing, and transfer after the locked SIM is discovered. The locked SIM is the decisive exit; APN repair, bill payment, and line resumption are not charged afterward. A SIM-first diagnostic order could omit some earlier troubleshooting.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0206\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0207\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The agent must distinguish several documented causes of no service and recognize that a missing SIM has a user fix while a locked SIM requires escalation; the other seeded faults do not override that mandatory exit.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0193\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0195\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0198\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0199\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"Customer lookup and user-guided device checks require selecting different tools and using their results to choose the next action; transfer itself takes a simple summary argument.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0322\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0490\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0540\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0524\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0434\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"Customer identification precedes support; diagnostic results determine whether to guide a fix or escalate. On the chosen path, reseating exposes the otherwise masked SIM lock, which then ends repair work. Transfer must precede its user-facing message; payment and APN prerequisites lie on excluded branches.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0563\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":2,\"rationale\":\"The supplied name and phone number support lookup, but the agent must obtain current device status rather than use judge-only setup facts. Ordinary successive checks can reveal the SIM condition.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0006\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0322\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0489\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0563\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"}]}},\"overall_score\":55,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"Transfer to a human for SIM security assistance while service remains unavailable, after establishing the locked-SIM condition; send the required transfer message after the call. This is an intended valid exit, not a claim of observed completion.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"A defensible sufficient path identifies John by phone, checks no-service indicators, turns off airplane mode if found on, checks the SIM, and guides reseating if it reports missing. A subsequent SIM check can establish the seeded PIN lock, triggering transfer. The SIM-first order is also defensible and may reach that finding with less preliminary work. Once the lock is established, neither the overdue-bill workflow nor APN repair is needed before the mandatory escalation.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Ratings of 2 workload, 3 reasoning, 2 tool use, 2 dependencies, and 2 information yield 5 × 11 = 55. The score reflects conditional troubleshooting before a supported escalation, not a full repair of every seeded fault.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"The missing-SIM setup can mask the PIN lock until reseating; the precise user-tool behavior after reseating is not supplied as an executed trace.\",\"The policies say both to try possible resolutions before transfer and to escalate a locked SIM. This assessment treats the specific locked-SIM instruction as the decisive exit, without requiring unrelated repairs first.\",\"Diagnostic order is not fixed; an airplane-mode check before a SIM check is plausible but not uniquely required.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"Reference supplies only the transfer call, not the diagnostic work needed to justify it.\",\"Baseline records and setup actions describe judge-only design state, not facts already known to the agent.\",\"The scenario example names get_status_bar, while the supplied user-tool contract names check_status_bar.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
